 "circuits": [
  {
   "id": "switching-test",
   "title": "Test circuit for switching time",
   "page": 6,
   "description": "Measures the switching times. A pulse generator drives the LED from pin 1; the cathode returns to ground through a monitor resistor RM, and the voltage across RM is the IF monitor. The phototransistor's collector is pulled up to VCC through the load resistor RL and is the output VO; the emitter is grounded. VO falls when IF turns on and comes back up when IF turns off; the four times are taken against the 10 % and 90 % levels of VO. The switching characteristics are specified at IC = 2 mA, VCE = 10 V, RL = 100 Ω.",
